::PC_U04_L05_Q_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U04_L05_Q_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.PA.8
Question:
Which feature distinguishes a hyperbola from an ellipse in item.
{
~A. A hyperbola has only positive squared terms#This choice uses a related idea but does not complete the required reasoning for the stated standard.
=C. A hyperbola has opposite signs between squared terms and uses asymptotes#Correct. This answer follows the lesson concept and connects the result to the stated standard.
~B. A hyperbola has no center#This choice reflects a common misconception or an incomplete step.
~D. A hyperbola is identified by a radius#This choice does not match the conditions in the question.
}

